usage: exp05_anchor [-h]
                    {info,make-plan,count-plan,dataset-spec,prepare-dataset,validate-dataset,get-case,run-case,run-index,run-plan,inspect-raw,missing-indices,analyze,validate}
                    ...

Experiment E5: certified root anchoring and safe pruning.

positional arguments:
  {info,make-plan,count-plan,dataset-spec,prepare-dataset,validate-dataset,get-case,run-case,run-index,run-plan,inspect-raw,missing-indices,analyze,validate}
    info                Report runtime and cryptographic support.
    make-plan           Generate a deterministic JSONL plan.
    count-plan          Count cases or work units in a plan.
    dataset-spec        Write the accumulator dataset specification.
    prepare-dataset     Build the read-only accumulator dataset.
    validate-dataset    Validate the prepared accumulator dataset.
    get-case            Extract one zero-based plan entry.
    run-case            Execute one case JSON file.
    run-index           Execute one zero-based plan entry.
    run-plan            Run all cases sequentially; intended for
                        smoke/reference only.
    inspect-raw         Audit raw result completeness and checks.
    missing-indices     Print comma-separated Slurm indices that need
                        recovery.
    analyze             Generate tables, figures, hypothesis checks, and
                        manifest.
    validate            Validate an analyzed result directory.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
